  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tigwirane Manja Counter - Trafficking in Persons Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Malawi):  USAID&apos;s Tigwirane Manja (translated as: lets join hands to fight human trafficking) Counter-Trafficking in Persons (C-TIP) activity will work to combat human trafficking in Malawi. Trafficking in Persons impacts on the rights of victims and their potential for full human development. This activity will focus on four key areas, namely prevention of trafficking in persons; improving the number of prosecutions of trafficking offenders; improving protection of survivors and management of shelters; and finally it will work to improve data collection and usage. The areas mentioned are part of the recommendations made in the 2020 State Department report for Malawi. By implementing these recommendations, the Government of Malawi and its partners will be able to deal with human trafficking issue..The Tigwirane Manja C-TIP activity will work with the National Coordinating Committee Against Trafficking in Person, a high-level ministerial committee headed by the Ministry of Homeland Security, and its civil society partners under the Malawi Network Against Human Trafficking. .The Tigwirane Manja C-TIP activity contributes to the Malawi ICS&apos;s Goal 3: Human Capital Development; and Objective 3.1 - Malawi improves individual and community agency to an extent that its citizens become more productive, engaged, and resilient. The activity also contributes to CDCS 2020-2025 DO 1/Intermediate Result 1.1 - citizens&apos; rights and responsibility actively exercised; DO 2/Intermediate Result 2.1 - youth agency and access to opportunities and services expanded; and, DO 3/Intermediate Result 3.1 - resilient people, households, communities, and systems manage and reduce vulnerabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
